+// Trimming of folded chamfer stripes (issue 032, lane R-032). See ChFi3d_Unfold.hxx for the class.
+//
+// Notation. A chamfer stripe is a chain of SurfData "pieces" along the spine abscissa W. The section
+// at W is the straight segment (ruling) L(W) = A(W) + s D(W), s in [0,1], from the contact point A(W)
+// on the other face (s = 0) to the contact point B(W) = A(W) + D(W) on the fold face F (s = 1).
+// Fold: B(W) moves against the spine direction on part of the spine. Then the contact curve on F
+// crosses itself at X_a = B(W_a) = B(W_b), W_a < W_b. The ridge is the set of points where two
+// rulings L(W) and L(W') (W < W') intersect; it is traced from (W_a, W_b, 1, 1) with W increasing
+// and W' decreasing, by Newton on A(W) + s D(W) - A(W') - s' D(W') = 0 (unknowns W', s, s'; three
+// equations). It ends
+//   E1: at W = W' (the two rulings coincide: pinch / swallowtail point of the ruled surface), reached
+//       by extrapolation of the traced branch in eps = W' - W (the ridge is smooth in eps);
+//   E3: at an apex X_m through which every ruling between W and W' passes (a circular arc of the
+//       spine with d_F > radius: the stripe there is a double cone).
+// Kept region of the stripe: s <= h(W) with h = 1 outside (W_a, W_b), the ridge on the two branches
+// and the apex in between. The piece containing W* (E1) is split along the ruling W* into two faces,
+// the second one on a copy of the surface (one pcurve per edge and surface). Everything else of the
+// result is kept; the contact curve on F is cut at X_a and its loop part is removed.
+// Any failure leaves the result untouched.
