+
+//! Trims folded chamfer stripes (internal to TKFillet, not exported).
+//!
+//! Class of the defect: a chamfer whose distance d_F measured on a support face F is larger than the
+//! radius of geodesic curvature of the spine on F where the spine turns toward the interior of F
+//! (d_F * kg > 1). The section of a chamfer is the segment between the points at distance d_F on F
+//! and d_O on the other face in the plane normal to the spine; along such a part of the spine the
+//! contact curve on F is the parallel curve at distance d_F, which passes the focal (evolute) point,
+//! reverses and crosses itself (a swallowtail). ChFi3d never trims a stripe against itself, so the
+//! face F gets a self-intersecting wire and the stripe folds over itself: an invalid solid.
+//!
+//! The correct chamfer removes the union of the section triangles. Its boundary is the ruled stripe
+//! cut at its self-intersection curve (the ridge, where two sections of the same stripe meet), which
+//! runs from the crossing point of the contact curve on F down to the point where the two sections
+//! coincide (a pinch / swallowtail point, W = W'), or to the apex shared by a whole family of sections
+//! (a circular arc of the spine with d_F > radius gives a cone whose sections all pass the apex).
+//! The contact curve on F is trimmed at the crossing point. The method is the exact trimming of a
+//! ruled surface self-intersection by pairs of intersecting rulings (Pekerman, Elber, Kim 2008;
+//! Farouki, Neff 1990; Pottmann, Wallner 2001), see issue 032 LITERATURE.
+//!
+//! Acts only on chamfer stripes (ChFiDS_ChamfSpine) whose contact curve reverses against the spine.
+//! On any failure the result is left exactly as built (no change). Returns true when theResult was
+//! replaced; the builder history (NewFaces, NewEdges, Splits, Merged) is updated for the new shapes.
+bool ChFi3d_UnfoldChamferStripes(const NCollection_List<occ::handle<ChFiDS_Stripe>>& theStripes,
+                                 const occ::handle<TopOpeBRepDS_HDataStructure>&     theDS,
+                                 const occ::handle<TopOpeBRepBuild_HBuilder>&        theCoup,
+                                 TopoDS_Shape&                                       theResult);
+
+#endif
